<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">FitzGeralds of Kildare</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Earls of Kildare, Geraldines of Kildare</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The FitzGeralds of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kildare">Kildare</a> were an Anglo-Norman family who held the earldom of Kildare from 1316, with their seat at Maynooth. In the late 15th and early 16th centuries Garret Mór and Garret Óg FitzGerald, as lords deputy, were the most powerful men in Ireland. The rebellion of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thomas-fitzgerald-10th-earl-of-kildare">Silken Thomas</a> in 1534–1535 broke their power, though the family survived.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/fitzgeralds-of-kildare.jpg" alt="FitzGeralds of Kildare" width="320" height="258" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sodacan · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coronet_of_a_British_Duke.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
